                                                                                rdfs:domain <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PhaseTapChangerAsymmetrical> ;
                                                                                rdfs:range <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#AngleDegrees> ;
                                                                                rdfs:comment "The phase angle between the inphase winding and the outof phase winding used for creating phase shift. The outofphase winding produces what is known as the difference voltage.  Setting this angle to 90 degrees is not the same as a symmetrical transformer. The attribute can only be multiples of 30 degrees.  The allowed range is 150 degrees to 150 degrees excluding 0." ;
                                                                                rdfs:label "windingConnectionAngle"@en .


