                                                                           rdfs:comment "Phase shift per step position. A positive value indicates a positive angle variation from the Terminal at the  PowerTransformerEnd  where the TapChanger is located into the transformer.The actual phase shift increment might be more accurately computed from the symmetrical or asymmetrical models or a tap step table lookup if those are available." ;
                                                                           rdfs:label "stepPhaseShiftIncrement"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PhaseTapChangerNonLinear.voltageStepIncrement
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PhaseTapChangerNonLinear.voltageStepIncrement> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                           rdfs:domain <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PhaseTapChangerNonLinear> ;
                                                                           rdfs:range <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PerCent> ;
                                                                           rdfs:comment "The voltage step increment on the out of phase winding the PowerTransformerEnd where the TapChanger is located specified in percent of rated voltage of the PowerTransformerEnd. A positive value means a positive voltage variation from the Terminal at the PowerTransformerEnd where the TapChanger is located into the transformer.When the increment is negative the voltage decreases when the tap step increases." ;
                                                                           rdfs:label "voltageStepIncrement"@en .


