                                                 rdfs:comment "Voltage at which the winding operates at the neutral tap setting. It is the voltage at the terminal of the PowerTransformerEnd associated with the tap changer when all tap changers on the transformer are at their neutralStep position.  Normally neutralU of the tap changer is the same as ratedU of the PowerTransformerEnd but it can differ in special cases such as when the tapping mechanism is separate from the winding more common on lower voltage transformers.This attribute is not relevant for PhaseTapChangerAsymmetrical PhaseTapChangerSymmetrical and PhaseTapChangerLinear. " ;
                                                 rdfs:label "neutralU"@en .


