                                                rdfs:label "ltcFlag"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.neutralStep
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.neutralStep> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                    rdfs:domain <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger> ;
                                                    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
                                                    rdfs:comment "The neutral tap step position for this winding.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal or less than highStep.It is the step position where the voltage is neutralU when the other terminals of the transformer are at the ratedU.  If there are other tap changers on the transformer those taps are kept constant at their neutralStep." ;
                                                    rdfs:label "neutralStep"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.normalStep
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.normalStep> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:domain <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger> ;
                                                   rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
                                                   rdfs:comment "The tap step position used in normal network operation for this winding. For a Fixed tap changer indicates the current physical tap setting.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal to or less than highStep." ;
                                                   rdfs:label "normalStep"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.step
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.step> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                             rdfs:domain <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger> ;
                                             rdfs:range xsd:float ;
                                             rdfs:comment "Tap changer position.Starting step for a steady state solution. Non integer values are allowed to support continuous tap variables. The reasons for continuous value are to support study cases where no discrete tap changer has yet been designed a solution where a narrow voltage band forces the tap step to oscillate or to accommodate for a continuous solution as input.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal to or less than highStep." ;
                                             rdfs:label "step"@en .


