<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredControllableLoad> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Temporary holding for load reduction attributes removed from RegisteredLoad. Use for future use case when developing the RegisteredDistributedResource specialized classes." ;
                                                        rdfs:label "RegisteredControllableLoad"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredDistributedResource
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredDistributedResource> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource> ;
                                                           rdfs:comment "A registered resource that represents a distributed energy resource such as a microgenerator fuel cell photovoltaic energy source etc. " ;
                                                           rdfs:label "RegisteredDistributedResource"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredGenerator
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredGenerator> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource> ;
                                                 rdfs:comment "Model of a generator  that is registered to participate in the market." ;
                                                 rdfs:label "RegisteredGenerator"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredInterTie
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredInterTie> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource> ;
                                                rdfs:comment "This class represents the inter tie resource." ;
                                                rdfs:label "RegisteredInterTie"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredLoad
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredLoad> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "Model of a load that is registered to participate in the market.RegisteredLoad is used to model any load that is served by the wholesale market directly. RegisteredLoads may be dispatchable or nondispatchable and may or may not have bid curves. Examples of RegisteredLoads would include distribution company load energy retailer load large bulk power system connected facility load.Loads that are served indirectly for example  through an energy retailer or a vertical utility should be modeled as RegisteredDistributedResources. Examples of RegisteredDistributedResources would include distribution level storage distribution level generation and distribution level demand response." ;
                                            rdfs:label "RegisteredLoad"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegisteredResource> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PowerSystemResource> ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A resource that is registered through the market participant registration system. Examples include generating unit load and nonphysical generator or load." ;
                                                rdfs:label "RegisteredResource"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegularIntervalSchedule
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegularIntervalSchedule> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#BasicIntervalSchedule> ;
                                                     rdfs:comment "The schedule has time points where the time between them is constant." ;
                                                     rdfs:label "RegularIntervalSchedule"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegularTimePoint
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegularTimePoint> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "Time point for a schedule where the time between the consecutive points is constant." ;
                                              rdfs:label "RegularTimePoint"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingCondEq
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingCondEq> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EnergyConnection> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "A type of conducting equipment that can regulate a quantity i.e. voltage or flow at a specific point in the network. " ;
                                              rdfs:label "RegulatingCondEq"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControl
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControl> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PowerSystemResource> ;
                                               rdfs:comment "Specifies a set of equipment that works together to control a power system quantity such as voltage or flow. Remote bus voltage control is possible by specifying the controlled terminal located at some place remote from the controlling equipment.The specified terminal shall be associated with the connectivity node of the controlled point.  The most specific subtype of RegulatingControl shall be used in case such equipment participate in the control e.g. TapChangerControl for tap changers.For flow control load sign convention is used i.e. positive sign means flow out from a TopologicalNode bus into the conducting equipment.The attribute minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue are required in the following cases For a power generating module operated in power factor control mode to specify maximum and minimum power factor values Whenever it is necessary to have an off center target voltage for the tap changer regulator. For instance due to long cables to off shore wind farms and the need to have a simpler setup at the off shore transformer platform the voltage is controlled from the land at the connection point for the off shore wind farm. Since there usually is a voltage rise along the cable there is typical and overvoltage of up 34 kV compared to the on shore station. Thus in normal operation the tap changer on the on shore station is operated with a target set point which is in the lower parts of the dead band.The attributes minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue are not related to the attribute targetDeadband and thus they are not treated as an alternative of the targetDeadband. They are needed due to limitations in the local substation controller. The attribute targetDeadband is used to prevent the power flow from move the tap position in circles hunting that is to be used regardless of the attributes minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue." ;
                                               rdfs:label "RegulatingControl"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControlModeKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControlModeKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "The kind of regulation model.   For example regulating voltage reactive power active power etc." ;
                                                       rdfs:label "RegulatingControlModeKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingLimit
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingLimit> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "This class represents the physical characteristic of a generator regarding the regulating limit." ;
                                             rdfs:label "RegulatingLimit"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Regulation
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Regulation> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#WorkDocument> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Special requirements andor regulations may pertain to certain types of assets or work. For example fire protection and scaffolding." ;
                                        rdfs:label "Regulation"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulationBranchKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulationBranchKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Kind of regulation branch for shunt impedance." ;
                                                  rdfs:label "RegulationBranchKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulationSchedule
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulationSchedule> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SeasonDayTypeSchedule> ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A preestablished pattern over time for a controlled variable e.g. busbar voltage." ;
                                                rdfs:label "RegulationSchedule"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RelativeDisplacement
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RelativeDisplacement> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Compound> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Vertical displacement relative to either sealevel ground or the center of the earth." ;
                                                  rdfs:label "RelativeDisplacement"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RelativeDisplacementKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RelativeDisplacementKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                      rdfs:comment "The types of relative displacement" ;
                                                      rdfs:label "RelativeDisplacementKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReliabilityInfo
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReliabilityInfo> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "Information regarding the experienced and expected reliability of a specific asset type of asset or asset model." ;
                                             rdfs:label "ReliabilityInfo"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemedialActionScheme
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemedialActionScheme> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PowerSystemResource> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Remedial Action Scheme RAS Special Protection Schemes SPS System Protection Schemes SPS or System Integrity Protection Schemes SIPS." ;
                                                  rdfs:label "RemedialActionScheme"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemedialActionSchemeKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemedialActionSchemeKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                      rdfs:comment "Classification of Remedial Action Scheme." ;
                                                      rdfs:label "RemedialActionSchemeKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteConnectDisconnectInfo
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteConnectDisconnectInfo> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Compound> ;
                                                         rdfs:comment "Details of remote connect and disconnect function." ;
                                                         rdfs:label "RemoteConnectDisconnectInfo"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteControl
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteControl> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemotePoint> ;
                                           rdfs:comment "Remote controls are outputs that are sent by the remote unit to actuators in the process." ;
                                           rdfs:label "RemoteControl"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteInputSignal
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteInputSignal> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> ;
                                               rdfs:comment "Supports connection to a terminal associated with a remote bus from which an input signal of a specific type is coming." ;
                                               rdfs:label "RemoteInputSignal"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemotePoint
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemotePoint> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> ;
                                         rdfs:comment "For an RTU remote points correspond to telemetered values or control outputs. Other units e.g. control centres usually also contain calculated values." ;
                                         rdfs:label "RemotePoint"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteSignalKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteSignalKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "Type of input signal coming from remote bus." ;
                                              rdfs:label "RemoteSignalKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteSource
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteSource> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemotePoint> ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Remote sources are state variables that are telemetered or calculated within the remote unit." ;
                                          rdfs:label "RemoteSource"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteUnit
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteUnit> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PowerSystemResource> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "A remote unit can be an RTU IED substation control system control centre etc. The communication with the remote unit can be through various standard protocols e.g. IEC 61870 IEC 61850 or non standard protocols e.g. DNP RP570 etc.. A remote unit contains remote data points that might be telemetered collected or calculated. The RemoteUnit class inherits PowerSystemResource. The intention is to allow RemoteUnits to have Measurements. These Measurements can be used to model unit status as operational out of service unit failure etc." ;
                                        rdfs:label "RemoteUnit"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteUnitType
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RemoteUnitType> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "Type of remote unit." ;
                                            rdfs:label "RemoteUnitType"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RepairItem
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RepairItem> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Asset component to be repaired or problem area to be corrected." ;
                                        rdfs:label "RepairItem"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RepairWorkTask
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RepairWorkTask> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#WorkTask> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "Work task for asset repair. Costs associated with this are considered corrective maintenance CM costs." ;
                                            rdfs:label "RepairWorkTask"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingCapability
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingCapability> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                                 rdfs:comment "font color0f0f0fDefinition of one set of reporting capabilities for this monitoring station. The associated EnvironmentalValueSets describe the maximum range of possible environmental values the station is capable of returning.  This attribute is intended primarily to assist a utility in managing its stations. font" ;
                                                 rdfs:label "ReportingCapability"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingGroup
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingGroup> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A reporting group is used for various adhoc groupings used for reporting." ;
                                            rdfs:label "ReportingGroup"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingMethodKind
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReportingMethodKind> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                 rdfs:comment "Method by which information is gathered from station." ;
                                                 rdfs:label "ReportingMethodKind"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RequestorRmrTest
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RequestorRmrTest> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "MPISO" ;
                                              rdfs:label "RequestorRmrTest"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveDemandCurve
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveDemandCurve> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Curve> ;
                                                rdfs:comment "Reserve demand curve.  Models maximum quantities of reserve required per Market Region and models a reserve demand curve for the minimum quantities of reserve. The ReserveDemandCurve is a relationship between unit operating reserve price in MWhr Yaxis and unit reserves in MW Xaxis." ;
                                                rdfs:label "ReserveDemandCurve"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveReq
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveReq> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceGroupReq> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Requirements for minimum amount of reserve andor regulation to be supplied by a set of qualified resources." ;
                                        rdfs:label "ReserveReq"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveReqCurve
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveReqCurve> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Curve> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A curve relating  reserve requirement versus time showing the values of a specific reserve requirement for each unit of the period covered. The  curve can be based on absolute time or on normalized time. X is time typically expressed in absolute timeY1 is reserve requirement typically expressed in MW" ;
                                             rdfs:label "ReserveReqCurve"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveRequirementType
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReserveRequirementType> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                    rdfs:comment "For exampleOperating Reserve Regulation Contingency" ;
                                                    rdfs:label "ReserveRequirementType"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Reservoir
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Reservoir> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PowerSystemResource> ;
                                       rdfs:comment "A water storage facility within a hydro system including ponds lakes lagoons and rivers. The storage is usually behind some type of dam." ;
                                       rdfs:label "Reservoir"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Resistance
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Resistance> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#CIMDatatype> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Resistance real part of impedance." ;
                                        rdfs:label "Resistance"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResistancePerLength
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResistancePerLength> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#CIMDatatype> ;
                                                 rdfs:comment "Resistance real part of impedance per unit of length." ;
                                                 rdfs:label "ResistancePerLength"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAssnType
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAssnType> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "For exampleAsset Owner Sink designator for use by CRRAsset Owner Source designator for use by CRRReliability Must Run  Scheduling Coordinator Load Serving Entity" ;
                                              rdfs:label "ResourceAssnType"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAwardClearing
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAwardClearing> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#MarketFactors> ;
                                                   rdfs:comment "Models details of bid and offer market clearing. Class indicates whether a contingency is active and whether the automatic dispatching system is active for this interval of the market solution." ;
                                                   rdfs:label "ResourceAwardClearing"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAwardInstruction
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceAwardInstruction> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                                      rdfs:comment "Model of market results instruction for resource.  Contains details of award as attributes." ;
                                                      rdfs:label "ResourceAwardInstruction"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceBid
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceBid> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Bid> ;
                                         rdfs:comment "Energy bid for generation load or virtual type for the whole of the markettrading period i.e. one day in day ahead market or one hour in the real time market." ;
                                         rdfs:label "ResourceBid"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCapacity
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCapacity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "This class model the various capacities of a resource. A resource may have numbers of capacities related to operating ancillary services energy trade and so forth. Capacities may be defined for active power or reactive power." ;
                                              rdfs:label "ResourceCapacity"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCapacityType
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCapacityType> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Resource capacity type." ;
                                                  rdfs:label "ResourceCapacityType"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCertification
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCertification> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Toplevel> ;
                                                   rdfs:comment "Specifies certification for a resource to participate in a specific markets." ,
                                                                "This class represent the resource certification for a specific product type. For example a resource is certified for NonSpinning reserve for RTM." ;
                                                   rdfs:label "ResourceCertification"@en .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCertificationCategory
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceCertificationCategory> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "ResourceCertificationCategory"@en .


