###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#OrientationKind.negative
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#OrientationKind.negative> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                               <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#OrientationKind> ;
                                                      rdfs:comment "For 2D diagrams a negative orientation gives the lefthand orientation favoured by computer graphics displays with X values increasing from left to right and Y values increasing from top to bottom.   This is also known as a left hand orientation." ;
                                                      rdfs:label "negative"@en .


